Synthesis of MSNs.  MSN was prepared by co-condensation method. CTAB $(500~\mathrm{mg})$ ) was dissolved in DI water $240~\mathrm{mL}$ ) followed by the addition of NaOH aqueous solution $\mathrm{1.50mL}$ , 2 M). The mixture was heated up to $80~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ under $\Nu_{2}$ in $500~\mathrm{mL}$ round bottomed flask with vigorous stirring. When the temperature became stable, TEOS $(2.5\mathrm{mL}$ ) was slowly added into the mixture solution via syringe. The mixture became turbid after adding TEOS, and was then stirred at 80 $^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for another $2\mathrm{h}$ . Afterwards, nanoparticles were collected by centrifugation at $8000\mathrm{rpm}$ for 10 min. The product was washed with MeOH, DI water and MeOH thoroughly. CTAB was removed by suspending the nanoparticles in MeOH ( $150~\mathrm{mL}$ ) containing HCl (3 mL, $37\%$ ). The mixture was refluxed at $80~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $24\mathrm{~h~}$ . The product MSNs were collected by centrifugation at 8000 rpm for 10 min and thoroughly washed by MeOH, water and MeOH.
Synthesis of PSNs. The polystyrene nanoparticles were prepared by soap-free polymerization in the presence of NaSS. Distilled $\mathrm{10~g}$ styrene, 0.0831 g KPS, $90~\mathrm{mL}$ water, and NaSS were charged into the reactor and then deoxygenated with $\Nu_{2}$ for $^{\textrm{1h}}$ . The reactant mixture was reacted at $70~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $24\mathrm{~h~}$ under $\Nu_{2}$ atmosphere. The obtained PSNs were dialyzed against water before further use.
Synthesis of MagNPs. $\mathrm{FeCl}_{3}{\cdot}6\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}$ $(2.4~\mathrm{g})$ and $\mathrm{FeCl}_{2}{\cdot}4\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}$ $\left(0.982\ \mathrm{g}\right)$ were dissolved in 10 mL DI water under $\Nu_{2}$ gas with vigorous stirring at $80~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ . Then, $5~\mathrm{mL}$ of ammonium hydroxide was added rapidly into the solution. The color of solution turned to black immediately. After 30 min, $3~\mathrm{mL}$ of oleic acid was added and the suspension was kept at $80~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $1.5\mathrm{h}$ . The obtained magnetite nanoparticles were washed with water and MeOH until pH became neutral. Magnetite nanoparticles $(0.5\ \mathrm{g})$ were added into $12~\mathrm{mL}$ water containing $10~\mathrm{mg}$ SDS, and the mixture in ice-water bath was treated with ultrasound for $10\ \mathrm{min}$ to obtain miniemulsion of magnetite nanoparticles. A styrene emulsion was prepared using $5~\mathrm{mL}$ styrene, $50~\mathrm{mg}$ SDS $40~\mathrm{mL}$ water, and $0.033~\mathrm{mL}$ tetradecane. Miniemulsion of magnetite nanoparticle and $5\mathrm{mg}\mathrm{KPS}$ were added to a three-neck flask and stirred for $30\mathrm{min}$ at $500{-}600~\mathrm{rpm}$ in $\mathrm{N}_{2}$ atmosphere. Afterwards, $10~\mathrm{mL}$ of styrene emulsion was added into the mixture, and the flask was placed in $80~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ water bath and maintained for $20\mathrm{~h~}$ to obtain MagNPs. This as-fabricated MagNPs was collected with a magnet and redispersed in $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}$ , and the collection-redispersion cycle was repeated three times before dispersing the MagNPs in 10 mL $_\mathrm{H_{2}O}$ for further usage.
Nanoparticle $@$ PDA core–shell nanoparticles. Typically, $50~\mathrm{mL}$ of as-synthesized $50\mathrm{nm}$ Au nanoparticles were centrifuged at 900 rcf for $15\mathrm{min}$ . Then, the pellets were redispersed in $2~\mathrm{mL}$ $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}.600~\upmu\mathrm{L}$ of the concentrated AuNPs was dispersed in $16~\mathrm{mL}$ TRIS buffer $\left(\mathrm{pH}8.5\right)$ , followed by adding $10~\mathrm{mg}$ dopamine. The reaction solution was stirred for $18\mathrm{~h~}$ and the purple product was purified by centrifugation. Similar procedure was applied to deposit PDA on other nanoparticles.
Synthesis of MagNP $@$ PDA $@$ AuNPs. MagNP $@$ PDA solution was injected into $50~\mathrm{mL}$ $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}$ at $85~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ under vigorous stirring. After 2 min, $4~\mathrm{mL}~0.1$ wt. $\%$ of $\mathrm{HAuCl}_{4}$ was injected into the solution. The reaction solution was stirred for $15~\mathrm{min}$ at $85~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ . The color of dispersion turned into dark brown first, and then became red finally. After purified by centrifugation, the obtained MagNP $@$ PDA $@$ AuNPs were stored in DMF.
Synthesis of ZIF-8 nanoparticles. Nanosized ZIF-8 particles were prepared by mixing $5~\mathrm{mL}$ MeOH solution of $Z_{\mathrm{{n}}}({\mathrm{NO}}_{3})_{2}$ $(12.5~\mathrm{mM})$ with 5 mL MeOH solution of 2-methylimidazole (25 mM). The mixture was shaken for $10~\mathrm{s}$ , and then allowed to react at room temperature for $12\mathrm{~h~}$ . The product was collected by centrifugation, washed several times with MeOH, and dried under vacuum overnight.
