Synthesis of UiO-66 nanoparticles. Nanosized UiO-66 particles were prepared by dissolving $4\ \mathrm{mM}\ Z\mathrm{r}\mathrm{Cl}_{4}$ and 4 mM $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{BDC}$ in a mixture of DMF and EtOH containing acetic acid. The reaction vial was capped and placed into an oven preheated at $100^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $12\mathrm{~h~}$ . The product was collected by centrifugation and then washed three times with DMF. The product was suspended in MeOH, and maintained at $60~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for three days. MeOH was renewed every $24\mathrm{~h~}$ to remove DMF. Finally, the product was washed 3 times with MeOH.
Synthesis of NP@PDA $@$ ZIF-8 nanoparticles. Typically, a predetermined amount of AuNP $@$ PDA in MeOH was added into 3 mL MeOH solution of $Z_{\mathrm{{n}}}({\mathrm{NO}}_{3})_{2}$ ( $12.5~\mathrm{mM},$ ), followed by 3 mL MeOH solution of 2-methylimidazole $25~\mathrm{mM},$ . The mixture was shaken for $10~\mathrm{s}$ , and then allowed to react at room temperature for 12 hours. The pink product was collected by centrifugation and washed 3 times with MeOH before dried under vacuum overnight. Similar procedure and conditions were used to coat ZIF-8 on other nanoparticles.
Synthesis of NP@PDA $@$ UiO-66 nanoparticles. Typically, a predetermined amount of AuNP $@$ PDA in DMF was added into a mixture of $4\ \mathrm{mM\ZrCl_{4}}$ and 4 mM $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{BDC}$ in a DMFEtOH $\mathrm{(v/v=}5{:}3\$ mixture. Afterwards, the solution was treated by ultrasonication for $10\ \mathrm{min}$ . Subsequently, the vial was capped and placed into an oven preheated at $100~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $12\mathrm{~h~}$ . The pink product was collected by centrifugation and then washed three times with DMF. The product was soaked in MeOH at $60~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for three days, and MeOH was renewed every $24\mathrm{~h~}$ to remove DMF. Finally, the product was washed 3 times with MeOH.
Catalytic study on 4-nitrophenol. The rate of catalytic reaction was determined using UV– vis spectroscopy. For this purpose, 4-nitrophenol ( $1.5\mathrm{\mL}$ , $0.2~\mathrm{mM}$ ) was mixed with fresh $\mathrm{NaBH_{4}}$ solution ( $1.5~\mathrm{mL}$ , $15~\mathrm{mM},$ . ${50}~\upmu\mathrm{L}$ of different catalysts were added into the reaction mixture at room temperature. The absorbance spectra was recorded in the range of $350~\mathrm{nm}$ to $800\mathrm{nm}$ .
Catalytic study on methylene blue. The rate of catalytic reaction was determined using UV– vis spectroscopy. For this purpose, methylene $(1.5~\mathrm{mL},8~\mathrm{mg/L})$ was mixed with fresh $\mathrm{NaBH_{4}}$ solution (1.5 mL, $15~\mathrm{mM}$ ). ${50\ \upmu\mathrm{L}}$ of different catalysts were added into the reaction mixture at room temperature. The absorbance spectra was recorded in the range of $400\mathrm{nm}$ to $750\mathrm{nm}$ .
